---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description={`Terms for using ${site.domain} and engaging ${site.name} for services.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h2 mt-3">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] text-ink-soft">Effective {site.termsEffective}</p>

      <div class="prose-site mt-8 text-ink-soft [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:mb-4 [&_li]:mb-1">
        <p>These terms cover your use of {site.domain} (the "Site") and, at a high level, how {site.legalName} ("{site.name}," "I," "we") works with clients. Specific engagements are governed by a written scope or agreement, which controls if it conflicts with anything here.</p>

        <h2>Using the Site</h2>
        <p>The Site is provided for information and to request services. Don't use it to send spam, scrape content, probe for vulnerabilities, or submit false information. Content on the Site belongs to {site.legalName} unless noted; you can share links to it freely.</p>

        <h2>How engagements work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Audit.</strong> A fixed-fee engagement (price quoted in writing before work starts), typically {site.auditDuration}, that ends in a written, prioritized plan. Payment is due before work starts unless the scope says otherwise.</li>
          <li><strong>Build.</strong> Fixed-scope work quoted from the audit. Changes to scope are quoted separately before they're done.</li>
          <li><strong>Operate.</strong> An optional monthly retainer, billed in advance, cancellable with 30 days' notice by either side.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="website-package">$799 website package</h2>
        <p>The $799 website package is a fixed-price service. It includes up to 6 pages written and designed for you, a mobile-friendly layout, a contact form that emails you each submission, one round of changes before the site goes live, and launch of the site.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Payment.</strong> The $799 is due in full before work starts, through the checkout link we send after you submit the signup form.</li>
          <li><strong>Timeline.</strong> Your site will be ready for you to review within 7 days of the date we have received your payment, your completed signup form, and your photos and logo. The 7 days do not start until we have all three.</li>
          <li><strong>Changes.</strong> One round of changes is included before the site goes live. A round is a single list of requested edits sent together. Further changes, new pages, and changes requested after the site goes live are quoted separately before any work is done.</li>
          <li><strong>Refund guarantee.</strong> If your site is not ready for review within the 7 days described above, or you review it and decide it isn't right for your business, tell us by email before the site goes live and we will refund the full $799. After the site goes live, the package is non-refundable. If you take a refund, the site does not go live and the design and copy stay with {site.legalName}.</li>
          <li><strong>Your domain and site.</strong> Your domain name is registered in your name and you own it. Yearly domain renewal fees are charged by the registrar and are your responsibility. Once the package is paid for and the site is live, the site's content and design are yours.</li>
          <li><strong>Hosting.</strong> Hosting is included at no charge. We can provide this because our hosting provider does not currently charge for it. If that changes, or if your site's traffic or features lead to hosting charges, we will give you at least 60 days' written notice by email before any hosting fee begins. You can then choose to pay the hosting fee, which will be no more than our cost plus a reasonable handling charge, or move your site to hosting of your choice. If you move, we will give you your site files at no charge.</li>
          <li><strong>What you provide.</strong> You are responsible for the accuracy of the information you give us, including license numbers and service claims, and for having the right to use the photos, logos, and videos you send.</li>
          <li><strong>Lead manager (optional).</strong> The lead manager is an optional monthly service. Nothing is charged for it at signup. The first monthly charge is 14 days after signup, a delay intended to keep billing from starting before your site goes live, and it then renews monthly. You can cancel any time, which stops future charges.</li>
          <li><strong>Owner video (optional).</strong> The owner video is an optional one-time purchase, priced separately and charged at checkout.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What you're responsible for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Providing access to the systems and data needed for the work, and having the right to grant that access.</li>
          <li>Reviewing deliverables and telling us promptly if something's off.</li>
          <li>Decisions about your business. Deliverables are recommendations and tools; you decide what to act on.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>No guarantee of results</h2>
        <p>Case studies and figures on the Site describe past work for specific clients. They are not a promise that your results will match. Revenue, ad performance, and email outcomes depend on many things outside our control. The refund guarantee for the $799 website package covers delivery and your approval of the site before it goes live. It is not a promise of leads, rankings, or sales.</p>

        <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>We keep client data and business information confidential and use it only to do the work. We don't name clients publicly without permission.</p>

        <h2>Ownership</h2>
        <p>Once paid for, deliverables built specifically for you (reports, workflows, spreadsheets, configurations) are yours. We keep the right to reuse general know-how, methods, and non-client-specific templates.</p>

        <h2>Third-party tools</h2>
        <p>Work often runs on platforms you own accounts with (Shopify, email platforms, Zapier, n8n, Google, Meta, and others). Their terms and pricing apply to you directly. We aren't responsible for their outages, changes, or fees.</p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, {site.legalName}'s total liability for any claim related to the Site or services is limited to the fees you paid for the specific engagement in question. We aren't liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including lost profits.</p>

        <h2 id="sms">SMS / text messaging terms</h2>
        <p><strong>Program:</strong> {site.legalName} ("{site.name}") customer-care messaging. When you opt in by checking the SMS consent box on a form at {site.domain}, or by calling or texting our business number, you agree to receive text messages from {site.name} about your inquiry: scheduling and reminders for calls, follow-up on your request, and updates on services you've asked about. We do not send promotional or marketing texts under this program.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Opting out:</strong> reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any message to cancel. You'll receive a single confirmation text and nothing further. You can also email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="link">{site.contactEmail}</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Help:</strong> reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message, or email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="link">{site.contactEmail}</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Message frequency varies</strong> by your request; typically a few messages around scheduling and follow-up.</li>
          <li><strong>Message and data rates may apply.</strong> Check with your carrier.</li>
          <li><strong>Carriers are not liable</strong> for delayed or undelivered messages.</li>
          <li>Consent to receive text messages is optional and not a condition of purchasing any service.</li>
          <li>How we handle your information, including that no mobile information is shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes, is described in our <a href="/privacy#sms" class="link">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arizona. Disputes will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Maricopa County, Arizona.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms; the effective date at the top will change when we do. Continued use of the Site after a change means you accept it.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>{site.legalName}<br />{site.mailingAddress}<br /><a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="link">{site.contactEmail}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
